p-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/232361\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":232362,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/232361\/revisions\/232362"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/232367"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=232361"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"companies_category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/companies_category?post=232361"},{"taxonomy":"subject","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/subject?post=232361"},{"taxonomy":"line_of_business","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/line_of_business?post=232361"},{"taxonomy":"topic","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/topic?post=232361"},{"taxonomy":"author","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/coauthors?post=232361"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":232245,"date":"2026-11-02T07:30:19","date_gmt":"2026-11-01T23:30:19","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/?p=232245"},"modified":"2026-11-02T09:51:19","modified_gmt":"2026-11-02T01:51:19","slug":"softening-rates-hong-kongs-ils-ambitions-indias-opening-market-to-dominate-in-singapore","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/softening-rates-hong-kongs-ils-ambitions-indias-opening-market-to-dominate-in-singapore\/","title":{"rendered":"Softening rates, Hong Kong&#8217;s ILS ambitions, India&#8217;s opening market to dominate in Singapore"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>The extent of softening, Hong Kong\u2019s ambitions as an alternative risk transfer hub and India\u2019s expanding reinsurance market will be among the major talking points as the industry gathers in Singapore this week.<\/p>\n<p>This year\u2019s Singapore International Reinsurance Conference (SIRC) is very much one for the market makers, with just the right conditions for the astute broker to feast upon: increasingly competitive market conditions, abundant capacity and growing demand for innovative risk transfer solutions across Asia.<\/p>\n<p>Here are the areas that I think are likely to dominate discussions in Singapore this year.<\/p>\n<h2>1. Pricing, attachment points<\/h2>\n<p>First and foremost, the direction of travel at forthcoming renewals will inevitably dominate discussions. Given that traditional capital has been replenished and alternative capacity continues to expand, cedents will be no doubt not only be seeking further improvements in pricing, but also in broader reinsurance structures.<\/p>\n<p>Expect multi-year deals, structured solutions, facilities and all that one would expect in a truly soft market to gather momentum at this year\u2019s conference as the APAC market confirms and underlines the direction of travel that <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/back-to-the-reinsurance-drawing-board-6-apac-takeaways-from-monte-carlo\/\">we saw in Monte Carlo in September.\u00a0<\/a><\/p>\n<p>For reinsurers, the challenge will be that clich\u00e9 of \u201cmaintaining underwriting discipline\u201d amid intensifying competition, particularly in property catastrophe business.<\/p>\n<p>I suspect that, despite the rhetoric, a fair bit of ground will be given here over the coming months, and the extent to which reinsurers are prepared to relax attachment points, broaden coverage or accept lower margins will be closely watched.<\/p>\n<h2>2. Managing nat cat risk<\/h2>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-229348 size-medium\" src=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-300x184.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"184\" srcset=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-300x184.png 300w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-1024x629.png 1024w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-150x92.png 150w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-768x472.png 768w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon-1536x943.png 1536w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/09\/zoom-earth-japan-typhoon.png 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px\" \/>This has been a particularly benign year in terms of natural catastrophe losses, and the lack of a major land-forming hurricane to hit the US this year is significant (though of course the season could still have a sting its tail).<\/p>\n<p>That said, natural catastrophe exposures will remain firmly on the agenda at SIRC, particularly given Asia\u2019s vulnerability to typhoons, flooding and other severe weather events. This year I think the conversation will be particularly interesting, especially given the growing take-up of more innovative solutions in the reinsurance space of late.<\/p>\n<p>As such, expect discussions to focus on the potential for parametric insurance, public-private partnerships and alternative capital to improve resilience in markets where insurance penetration remains low.<\/p>\n<p>The growing significance of secondary perils and attritional catastrophe losses is also likely to feature prominently, alongside continuing concerns over whether existing models adequately capture changing exposures.<\/p>\n<h2>3. Merger fervour<\/h2>\n<p>The P&amp;C (re)insurance market has experienced a wave of M&amp;A activity this year, spread across the sector, involving specialty insurers, Lloyd\u2019s syndicates and Japanese insurance groups. To date, we\u2019ve had Zurich\u2019s US$10.9billion takeover of Beazley, Sompo\u2019s US$3.5 billion move for Aspen, AIG\u2019s investment in Convex, and Starr\u2019s acquisition of IQUW.<\/p>\n<p>With no signs of the soft market changing direction any time soon, and impatient investors keen to make some decent returns, expect more of the same\u2026 with APAC very much in the limelight!<\/p>\n<h2>4. Indian market maturity<\/h2>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-230102 size-medium\" src=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--300x184.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"184\" srcset=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--300x184.png 300w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--1024x629.png 1024w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--150x92.png 150w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--768x472.png 768w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity--1536x943.png 1536w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/india-full-capacity-.png 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px\" \/>It has been a long time coming, but the once relatively closed-off Indian market is finally opening up to international investment on the reinsurance side. The development of Gujarat International Finance Tec-City (Gift City) is attracting growing international interest, as regulatory and tax incentives attract international reinsurers seeking access to India\u2019s domestic market and opportunities elsewhere in Asia.<\/p>\n<p>Indeed, reinsurance premium written through Gift City\u2019s international financial services centre has increased more than fourfold to approximately US$608 million in the 2025\u201326 financial year.<\/p>\n<p>Expect chatter at SIRC about how far demand for reinsurance is expected to increase across property catastrophe, agriculture, infrastructure, health and specialty lines as India\u2019s economy develops and insurance coverage expands. However, questions still remain about pricing adequacy and the adequacy of catastrophe modelling.<\/p>\n<h2>Hong Kong\u2019s ambitions<\/h2>\n<p>Hong Kong\u2019s desire to establish itself as a leading regional reinsurance and alternative risk transfer hub are also likely to be a key talking point at SIRC.<\/p>\n<p>In September, the <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/hong-kong-pushes-captive-insurance-ils-reforms-as-policy-address-seeks-to-strengthen-international-hub-status\/\">territory\u2019s government unveiled proposals<\/a> to introduce protected cell company structures, designed to reduce the costs of establishing captive insurers and issuing insurance-linked securities (ILS).<\/p>\n<p>The government also plans to review restrictions on ILS investors and expand catastrophe risk transfer capacity. Singaporean authorities will no doubt be watching with interest how this all plays out!<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Attendees will focus on competitive pricing and broader structures, nat cat and parametric solutions, M&#038;A momentum, and the rise of India&#8217;s Gift City and Hong Kong as regional reinsurance hubs.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":5714,"featured_media":232256,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"companies_category":[],"subject":[],"line_of_business":[],"topic":[187],"coauthors":[553],"class_list":["post-232245","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","post_category-analysis","post_category-whitelist","topic-sirc"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.6 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Softening rates, Hong Kong&#039;s ILS ambitions, Ind