tps:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=232328"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/232328\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":232359,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/232328\/revisions\/232359"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/232331"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=232328"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"companies_category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/companies_category?post=232328"},{"taxonomy":"subject","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/subject?post=232328"},{"taxonomy":"line_of_business","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/line_of_business?post=232328"},{"taxonomy":"topic","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/topic?post=232328"},{"taxonomy":"author","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/coauthors?post=232328"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":232255,"date":"2026-10-31T08:00:11","date_gmt":"2026-10-31T00:00:11","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/?p=232255"},"modified":"2026-11-02T08:34:17","modified_gmt":"2026-11-02T00:34:17","slug":"looking-beyond-market-cycles","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/looking-beyond-market-cycles\/","title":{"rendered":"Looking beyond market cycles"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><i><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Welcome to Full Capacity, a weekly briefing on all the most important developments of the past week with a personal take on the news from our editor-in-chief,\u00a0Mithun\u00a0Varkey, delivered to your inbox every Saturday.<\/span><\/i><span data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f\u202f<\/span><span data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">New coverholder<\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">. Dubai-based MGA <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/elseco-expands-into-asia-with-singapore-ah-lloyds-coverholder-launch\/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">elseco has launched a Lloyd&#8217;s Asia coverholder<\/span><\/a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> in Singapore, initially writing A&amp;H business under Lisa Leow, InsuranceAsia News first reported. Elseco has also secured general aviation capacity from Ping An P&amp;C, expanding its aviation and space specialism.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Government backstop. <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">South Korea is set to <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/onshore-captives-third-party-capital-primed-for-rapid-growth-in-apac-blackrock\/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">introduce a state-backed reinsurance program<\/span><\/a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> for storm, flood and earthquake insurance. The state will conclude reinsurance agreements with insurers and the national treasury will operate as the insurer of last resort, according to the legislative amendment bill reviewed by InsuranceAsia News.\u00a0<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Buying time. <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Indian insurance regulator has <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/irdai-extends-deadline-for-insurance-distribution-reform-feedback-to-october-31\/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">extended the deadline for submitting feedback<\/span><\/a><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> on proposed distribution reforms to Saturday. The consultation has received over 650 comments received so far.\u00a0<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Last month, the regulator released a two-part consultation paper on the <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/brokers-warn-indias-distribution-reform-plan-risks-job-cuts-sector-disruption\/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">proposed distribution reforms<\/span><\/a><span data-contrast=\"auto\">, which has seen resistance from brokers and insurers.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Evolving priorities. <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Captive reinsurance and utilisation of third-party capital are <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/onshore-captives-third-party-capital-primed-for-rapid-growth-in-apac-blackrock\/\">\u201ctop of mind\u201d for insurers<\/a> in Asia Pacific amid the ongoing evolution of regulatory capital regimes across the region, Mark Erickson, global insurance strategist with BlackRock\u2019s financial institutions group, told InsuranceAsia News.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">New branding. <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Envest Agencies will become Orvia Australia and New Zealand as parent firm Ardonagh <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/envest-agencies-rebrands-hires-belinda-steedman-as-ceo\/\"><span data-contrast=\"none\">rebranded its global MGA businesses<\/span><\/a><span data-contrast=\"auto\">. Orvia Australia and New Zealand will be led by newly appointed CEO Belinda Steedman, who joins from Aviva.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0px;\">(Re)draw, (re)map, (re)align <\/span><\/p>\n<div>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The reinsurance renewal season is in full swing, and next week it will shift up a gear as the global industry descends on Singapore for the region\u2019s marquee event: the Singapore International Reinsurance Conference (SIRC).<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The 22nd edition of the annual summit is set to be its biggest yet, drawing delegates from more than 80 countries. This year\u2019s theme, \u201cCapacity to Capability,\u201d captures a simple but important idea: reinsurers can offer more than capital.\u00a0<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The headline from the conference is likely to be familiar \u2013 record capacity, further softening, reinsurers preaching underwriting discipline, and cedents and intermediaries pushing for greater flexibility.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">But beyond the familiar ratings and capacity narrative, more consequential forces are reshaping the market.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The hard market, together with the rising frequency and severity of climate-related events, undoubtedly reset industry dynamics. Yet that reset proved relatively short-lived and largely specific to the world of (re)insurance.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">As 2026 draws to a close, it is increasingly clear that the industry is operating in a world in transition \u2013 above all in technology and geopolitics.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The war in the Middle East has remapped trade routes and redrawn geopolitical equations in ways rarely seen in recent decades. Its impact has been prolonged, and there is no easy end in sight.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Meanwhile, AI, semiconductors and data centres are changing the rules of business and economics \u2013 perhaps irreversibly.\u00a0<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The acceleration in AI capability and adoption this year marks a definitive shift, realigning economic fortunes in ways the industry has yet to fully understand.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Whether it is geopolitical turmoil or technological upheaval, Asia sits at the centre of both.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Japan\u2019s technology-led investment boom is a case in point. Private non-residential investment has reached approximately 19% of GDP this year, its highest level since 1991. While it has not yet reached the scale of Japan\u2019s late-1980s investment boom, it is substantial.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">South Korea, Taiwan and China, meanwhile, are emerging as central players in the global AI and semiconductor race.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For insurers and their clients, the implications go well beyond traditional property covers. Business interruption, contingent liabilities and the transfer of supply-chain risk are moving rapidly up the priority list.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">This renewal season may therefore mark the beginning of a longer-term shift: not merely in pricing and capacity, but in the design of insurance programs and in the role reinsurers are expected to play.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">The industry has capacity. The question now is whether it has the capability to underwrite a changing world.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:276}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">To keep up with all the action at the region\u2019s biggest industry event, InsuranceAsia News has assembled its most extensive SIRC coverage ever.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"auto\">For in-depth insights and market colour straight from the conference floor, pick up a copy of our daily newspaper at the event and follow our comprehensive coverage online, including breaking news, exclusive interviews and expert analysis, all unlocked for you.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0px;\">People moves<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Starr <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">has appointed<\/span><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> Zoe Xie <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">as head of distribution and strategic initiatives for Asia Pacific<\/span><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">.<\/span><\/b><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Sompo <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">has tapped <\/span><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Azra Amir <\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">for head of operations in Australia.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">WTW<\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> has named <\/span><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Greg Solomon<\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> as market leader for its insurance consulting and technology business.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Bajaj General Insurance<\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> has appointed <\/span><b><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Deepak Reddy<\/span><\/b><span data-contrast=\"auto\"> to succeed Tapan Singhel as managing director and CEO.<\/span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">Do check out our<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">weekly<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f<\/span><a style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/bajaj-general-insurance-lloyds-orvia-sompo-11-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week\/\"><b><span data-contrast=\"none\">people move round-up<\/span><\/b><\/a><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">to<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">\u202f<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-contrast=\"auto\">stay up to speed on the most important appointments in the region.<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>This week&#8217;s newsletter also discusses a new Lloyd&#8217;s Asia coverholder, South Korea&#8217;s new reinsurance program, India&#8217;s distribution reforms, APAC insurers&#8217; evolving priorities and Envest Agencies&#8217; rebranding. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":6035,"featured_media":232270,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"companies_category":[],"subject":[],"line_of_business":[],"topic":[187],"coauthors":[534],"class_list":["po