people-moves-of-the-week","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/bajaj-general-insurance-lloyds-orvia-sompo-11-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week\/","title":{"rendered":"Bajaj General Insurance, Lloyd&#8217;s, Orvia, Sompo: 11 APAC insurance people moves of the week"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>InsuranceAsia News wraps up the people moves from the insurance industry in Asia this week.<\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">1. Bajaj General Insurance names new CEO, managing director<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Bajaj General Insurance<\/strong> has appointed <strong>Deepak Reddy<\/strong> to succeed Tapan Singhel as managing director and CEO, with the board of Bajaj Finserv having approved Reddy\u2019s appointment, effective from January 1.<\/p>\n<p>He replaces Singhel, who is stepping down in accordance with the IRDAI\u2019s maximum continuous tenure of 15 years for managing directors, CEOs and whole-time directors.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/bajaj-general-insurance-names-deepak-reddy-as-new-ceo-and-managing-director\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">2. Lloyd\u2019s China unveils new leadership team as regulator approves appointments<\/h2>\n<p>The Shanghai bureau of the National Financial Regulatory Administration cleared <strong>Furen Shen<\/strong>\u2019s appointment as chief executive officer earlier this month.<\/p>\n<p>Shen, a <strong>Lloyd<\/strong>\u2019s China veteran who joined in 2010, steps up from interim CEO after taking the role on April 1, succeeding Yuanbiao Sun, who has been elevated to chairman.<\/p>\n<p>Sun had stepped down as CEO earlier this year to become a non-executive director, before the regulator approved his move to the top board role last month.<\/p>\n<p>The regulator also approved Xiaolan Li as chief compliance officer last week, completing the platform\u2019s new senior leadership line-up.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/lloyds-china-unveils-new-leadership-team-as-regulator-approves-appointments\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">3. Envest Agencies rebrands, hires CEO<\/h2>\n<p>Envest Agencies will become <strong>Orvia<\/strong> Australia and New Zealand as parent firm Ardonagh rebranded its global MGA businesses Orvia Underwriting.<\/p>\n<p class=\"news-title\">Orvia Australia and New Zealand, will be led by newly appointed CEO <strong>Belinda Steedman<\/strong>, who has 30 years of insurance experience and was most recently Aviva\u2019s director of global proposition.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/envest-agencies-rebrands-hires-belinda-steedman-as-ceo\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">4. Sompo taps Australia head of operations <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-thumbnail wp-image-232237 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Azra-Amir-150x150.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" srcset=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Azra-Amir-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Azra-Amir-300x300.png 300w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Azra-Amir.png 501w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px\" \/><\/h2>\n<p><strong>Sompo<\/strong> has appointed <strong>Azra Amir<\/strong> as its head of operations in Australia.<\/p>\n<p>Sydney-based Amir has joined from Aon, where she had been head of process excellence for Asia Pacific since February 2023.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span>\u00a0<a style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/sompo-taps-azra-amir-as-head-of-operations-in-australia\/\">here.<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">5. WTW appoints Hong Kong ICT market leader<\/h2>\n<p><strong>WTW<\/strong> has named <strong>Greg Solomon<\/strong> as market leader for its insurance consulting and technology (ICT) business in Hong Kong.<\/p>\n<p>He has rejoined WTW to replace Sean Deehan, who left in July to take over as APAC CEO of Aon\u2019s Strategy and Technology Group.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/greg-solomon-rejoins-wtw-as-hong-kong-ict-market-leader\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">6. Marsh names lead for newly-formed captive strategy<\/h2>\n<p><span class=\"l4jgb5 l4jln8\"><span class=\"l4jln8\" data-sdui-anchor-id=\"commentary-HVMbXZR5Rs1B9n15TDXH9kJSNxR6dbbZPZ09J7SjJrY-cf28c44f-91b6-4dfd-8cc6-2fb0a52db8ac::179\"><strong>Marsh<\/strong> has promoted <strong>Shawn Willis<\/strong><\/span><\/span> to the newly-created role of captive strategy leader for the Pacific.<\/p>\n<p>The newly created role is focused on helping Marsh&#8217;s clients evaluate, optimise, and build long-term captive strategies aligned to their risk and business objectives.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<\/span><a style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\" href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/marsh-promotes-shawn-willis-to-lead-newly-formed-captive-strategy\/\">here.<\/a><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">7. Lockton expands in New Zealand with Wellington office, Marsh and WTW hires<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Lockton<\/strong> has expanded its New Zealand operations with the opening of a Wellington office, hiring Marsh\u2019s <strong>Felix Ukaegbu<\/strong> as general manager and adding <strong>James Earwaker<\/strong> from WTW as client director for financial lines.<\/p>\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ukaegbu and Earwaker join Wellington-based Graham Elliot, who joined Lockton earlier this year as a client director in its people solutions business.<\/p>\n<p>Ukaegbu joins from Marsh, where he has served as chief client officer for risk management in New Zealand, and has been based in Wellington since 2024, while Earwaker, who was most recently Wellington and central manager at WTW, has more than 20 years of industry experience in financial, executive and professional risks.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/lockton-expands-in-new-zealand-with-wellington-office-marsh-and-wtw-hires\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">8. Starr appoints APAC head of distribution, strategic initiatives <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-232232\" src=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Starr-Zoe-Xie-150x150.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" srcset=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Starr-Zoe-Xie-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Starr-Zoe-Xie-300x300.png 300w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Starr-Zoe-Xie-768x768.png 768w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Starr-Zoe-Xie.png 1000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px\" \/><\/h2>\n<p><strong>Starr<\/strong> has appointed Zoe Xie as head of distribution and strategic initiatives for Asia Pacific.<\/p>\n<p>Singapore-based Xie joins from Axa XL, where she was most recently head of property since March 2024, and was also briefly the interim head of the corporate business division for China between July 2025 and March.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/starr-names-zoe-xie-as-apac-head-of-distribution-strategic-initiatives\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">9. Elseco names head as part of expansion into Asia<\/h2>\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dubai-based specialty MGA <strong>elseco<\/strong> has expanded into Asia with the launch of a Lloyd\u2019s Asia coverholder in Singapore, with the new operation to be led by <strong>Lisa Leow<\/strong> as head of A&amp;H for Asia.<\/p>\n<p style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Elseco Asia will begin by writing accident and health (A&amp;H) business and will operate under the Lloyd\u2019s Asia Scheme in Singapore.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/elseco-expands-into-asia-with-singapore-ah-lloyds-coverholder-launch\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">10. Echo Re strengthens Gift City team with underwriting manager appointment<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Echo Re<\/strong> has appointed <strong>Sanjana Sinha<\/strong> as an underwriting manager for its Gujarat International Finance Tech-City (Gift City) branch.<\/p>\n<p>Sinha joins the reinsurer after spending 12 years with Axa XL in Gurugram, last holding the position of underwriting manager since April 2024.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/echo-re-adds-sanjana-sinha-to-gift-city-team-as-underwriting-manager\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2 class=\"news-title\">11. Chaucer names APAC lead underwriter for agriculture <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-thumbnail wp-image-232238 alignleft\" src=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Jay-Bae-150x150.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" srcset=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Jay-Bae-150x150.png 150w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Jay-Bae-300x300.png 300w, https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/10\/Jay-Bae.png 501w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px\" \/><\/h2>\n<p><strong>Chaucer Group<\/strong> has appointed <strong>Jay Bae<\/strong> as its lead underwriter for agriculture for Asia Pacific.<\/p>\n<p>Singapore-based Bae joins from Swiss Re, where he was most recently the head of agriculture for Southeast Asia, Australia, New Zealand, Japan and South Korea since October 2023.<\/p>\n<p><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Read the full story<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/ergo-insurance-appoints-prasirt-rerkumnuaychok-as-chief-distribution-officer\/\">here<\/a>.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2>Other moves you may have missed<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Yusuke Matsumoto<\/strong>, <strong>S<\/strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\"><strong>wiss Re<\/strong>\u2019s head of facultative reinsurance for APAC, is <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/swiss-res-apac-facultative-reinsurance-head-yusuke-matsumoto-confirms-singapore-relocation\/\">set to relocate<\/a> from Japan to Singapore this week. <\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Tokyo-based Matsumoto succeeded <\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">Ronnie Tong in May<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\">,<\/span><span style=\"letter-spacing: 0px;\"> having served as interim since April.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Beazley<\/strong>\u2019s <strong>Stefan Bramwell<\/strong> has <a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/beazleys-stefan-bramwell-relocates-to-singapore-for-energy-underwriter-role\/\">relocated from London to Singapore<\/a> to take on the role of energy underwriter. Bramwell has been with Beazley since May 2024, having returned from an 18-month career break.<\/p>\n<p><em>For more InsuranceAsia News (IAN) people moves at brokers, insurers, reinsurers, insurtechs, specialty players, MGAs and loss adjusters across Asia Pacific\u2019s fast-growing (re)insurance markets click\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/post_category\/people\/\">here<\/a>.<\/em><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>WTW, Marsh, Lockton, Starr, Elseco, Echo Re and Chaucer also made personnel changes over the last week.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":11026,"featured_media":232235,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"companies_category":[],"subject":[],"line_of_business":[],"topic":[],"coauthors":[882],"class_list":["post-232186","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","post_category-people-moves","post_category-whitelist"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.6 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/product\/yoast-seo-wordpress\/ -->\n<title>Bajaj General Insurance, Lloyd&#039;s, Orvia, Sompo: 11 APAC insurance people moves of the week<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The key resource for accurate, insightful and reliable coverage of Asia\u2019s insurance and reinsurance market.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/bajaj-general-insurance-lloyds-orvia-sompo-11-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Bajaj General Insurance, Lloyd&#039;s, Orvia, Sompo: 11 APAC insurance people moves of the week\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The key resource for accurate, insightful and reliable coverage of Asia\u2019s insurance and reinsurance market.\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/insuranceasianews.com\/bajaj-general-